I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's declared contract grants only `inference-llm`, and the graph definition hasn't been updated yet. Sending each item's text to an external host would also expose feed content to a network destination the node isn't scoped for, and building a URL from unescaped feed text would be an injection risk. The classifier below uses only `inference-llm` and produces the same output as specified.

```wit
package gen:node;

use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

world node {
    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

